n  getting  suddenly more support for our Dragon  Ball super content so I want to give you  a big thank you for that if you enjoy  these videos and want to see more be  sure to leave a like to let me know and  if you are new to the channel don't  forget to subscribe and hit that  notification bell there are two quick  points to keep in mind that could  potentially explain some of the reason  why kefla was able to beat Super Saiyan  blue Goku one is the fact that Goku  after just having fought jiren a short  time earlier is still trained and far  below 100% strength and the other is  that Kael possesses the berserk  Super Saiyan power that is different  from the power of ordinary super safe  many have assumed that Kael strength in  her berserk form can be compared to  broli because his legendary Super Saiyan  form is so similar to kales berserk form  but because Broly is technically not  canon kales power could theoretically be  far greater than Broly at this point  nevertheless I agree that it does seem  outlandish that the Saiyans of universe  6 have been getting stronger so quickly  and many fans have said that this is  just plot convenience pure and simple  and while I am sure that plot  convenience is definitely a part of it  since it wouldn't be very fun for us to  watch the universe 6 saying struggling  for years in order to catch up to the  universe 7 Saiyans believe it or not  there are logical reasons as to why  Khalif law kale and Kaabah are growing  so much faster than to the universe 7  sayings in order to explain these  reasons I will use real-world examples  of similar things actually happening in  real life and while I can't say that  these reasons explain everything and  that plot convenience doesn't also play  a part the reasons I give you just might  make you feel a bit different about the  rapid growth that we've been seeing from  the universe 6 and especially  cauliflower and kale the first real-life  example I want to talk about is what is  known as the four-minute mile back in  the 1950s it was considered impossible  for a human being to run the distance of  a mile in less than  four minutes while many athletes had  gotten close to running a mile in four  minutes no one had succeeded in breaking  that barrier during an official  competition it got to the point that  many coaches sports experts and even  doctors said that it was simply  impossible for a human body to run a  mile in less than four minutes they even  warned that trying to do it could cause  serious physical damage to your body and  then one day in 1954 an athlete by the  name of Roger Bannister broke the  barrier and ran a mile in just a few  seconds under four minutes within a week  of Roger Bannister breaking the record  five other runners also did it within a  year fifty-four athletes from around the  world broke the barrier and only a few  years later even high school track and  field runners have begun to break the  four-minute barrier so how was this  possible for decades if not centuries  people believed it was physically  impossible to break this barrier and  then suddenly a ton of people are doing  it but that's just it as soon as the  first person succeeded as soon as Roger  Bannister showed the world that it could  be done that it was possible other  athletes were inspired to push  themselves and they also succeeded they  broke through the mental barrier of what  they thought was possible and suddenly  they were achieving the impossible the  same logic can be applied to Dragon Ball  super the universe 7 Saiyans didn't have  anyone else to show them what was  possible when Goku became a Super Saiyan  he was the first Super Saiyan any of our  main characters had ever seen before  that only legends told of the existence  of Super sands but no one knew it was  truly possible until they saw it with  their own eyes the universe seven  Saiyans essentially stumbled upon new  forms and transformations as a result of  extreme training or extremely powerful  emotions like rage however until  extraordinary threats forced them to  train so hard or put them in a situation  where their emotions took over they had  no concept of higher forms even existing  on the other hand the universe six  Saiyans saw what was possible from  watching the universe 7 Saiyans  Goku and the others were to the universe  six Saiyans what roger bannister was to  the runners of the 1950's once they knew  that new forms and transformations  existed and could be reached the  universe six sands were inspired to  strive towards reaching them to focus  directly on that goal and for this  reason they were able to attain them  more quickly the universe seven Saiyans  broke the mental barrier that told the  universe 6 Saiyans that they could only  progress so far and once these barriers  were broken everything changed  if we combine the breaking of this  mental barrier with the unique feature  of the Saiyan race which is of course  far more competitive and physically  powerful than ordinary humans then this  begins to explain why the Saiyans of  universe 6 have gotten stronger so much  quicker than the universe 7 Saiyans  the second real-life example that I  would like to bring up is the concept of  talent hot spots in a book called the  talent code author Daniel Coyle argues  that small communities of people who are  working intensely towards the same or  similar goals develop incredible talent  and skill far more quickly than they  would if they were trying to progress on  their own for example during the  Renaissance the center of this great  rebirth that took place throughout  Europe was the small Italian city of  Florence in this one city of only about  60,000 people a huge number of the  world's greatest artists appeared  including Donatello Botticelli Raphael  Michelangelo and Leonardo da Vinci along  with many others all of these incredibly  talented people were either born in or  lived in Florence during the Renaissance  so why 